# Half-Life crowbar. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# Part J: "A physical object with mass. Hits are found by sweeping the
# crowbar's head (declared in the card) between consecutive commands against
# hitboxes and the world, on the server; damage scales with the head's speed
# at contact, with a floor below which nothing happens."
#
# NO JOINTS, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE WEAPON. A crowbar has nothing that moves
# relative to itself. What it has is a head, and the head is the card's only
# real content - the tool found `BoxEnd`, three vertices sitting at the end
# of the bar, which is exactly the marker a card wants.
#
# The numbers are a floor and a cap. Below the floor the bar is being carried
# rather than swung and nothing happens; at the cap it does its full damage,
# and faster does not do more - so a swing amplified by a tracking glitch
# cannot one-shot anything.

weapon v_crowbar
match  bones 32  seqs 11  hash 0xd4b0a53b

strike point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 3.0  from 60  full 260

# Part J also asks for prying: "Wedge the tip into a breakable vent, grate or
# crate and lever it: sustained torque applies damage until it gives." The
# tip is the same point as the head on this model, and the levering itself is
# not built yet, so no pry point is declared - a declared one that nothing
# acts on would be a promise the weapon does not keep.
